{"kind":"artifact","text":"The serving page stops asserting the reasoning this lane disproved. Exact clean pushed head f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be on request/repo-remote-link; tree f08ef41f, checkout clean, origin matching, base equals current main c679fb73. Under planner's current-basis request eb034253 and my promise 8abe2015.\n\nTHE SENTENCE THIS LANE WROTE AND THIS HEAD CORRECTS. 'The remote is read from the repository's own configuration only — git config --local — so configuration outside the repository cannot say where the repository lives.' Not inherited prose: the lane added it, in the same block that introduced the feature. So correcting it is finishing a sentence the lane started, which is the ground planner's ruling 9dfac278 granted it on, alongside this path already being in the seven-path set.\n\nIt now states both bounds and why neither implies the other.\n\nONE SENTENCE DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED, and I am naming it so a reviewer sees it was checked rather than missed. 'A URL carrying userinfo, a query or a fragment is declined outright rather than stripped' was false when this lane wrote it, because Go silently normalised away a bare trailing '#' instead of declining it. The raw-delimiter fix makes it true as written. The code caught up to the sentence rather than the sentence needing to catch up to the code.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached — cmd/gs 229.171s, internal/kernel 157.364s, internal/app 157.137s, internal/docset 99.737s. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet and diff-check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be","path":"docs/reference/gs/serve.md"}}